Z||000000||mrfixit58||07-18-2000||08:57 PM||||Some of you may remember, a few months ago I sold my project 87 GT to my Brother-in-Law and began the search which, ultimatly, landing me my Blue 87 GT. Well, a couple of months and about $3600 later, my Bro-n-laws 87 GT is ready to hit the show circuit. So, without further ado...<P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rightfrntjpg_1.jpg"> <P>After:<BR>[img]http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/left frnt_1.jpg[/img]<P>Before:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/leftrear.jpg"> <P>After:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lftrear.jpg"> <P>Before:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieropasseat.jpg"> <P>After:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/interior_2.jpg"> <P>THe color is Viper Red, the interior seat covers, headliner, sunvusors, door pockets, and shift boot are Mr. Mikes, the 1/4 windows are from fieroshop.<P>While riding it the other day, I watched a guy in a C-5 Corvette, crane his head almost all the way around to try and get a better look as we passed in the other direction. The car is BEAUTIFUL!<P>Just thought you guy whould enjoy the pics,<BR>Roy<P>||||reg||14
Z||000001||Cooter||07-18-2000||09:01 PM||||WOW!||||reg||14
