Z||000005||Formula||07-18-2000||09:26 PM||||how were the wheels refinished?....is that paint or just sanded down?<P>EXCELLENT JOB.....and I mean EXCELLENT!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000006||mrfixit58||07-18-2000||09:32 PM||||The outer portion was polished. The spokes were bead blasted and painted with the same paint as the ground effects except with additional metal flake. When I first saw them, I thought the were aftermarket. I liked them so much that I asked him to get the formula from his painter.<P>Roy||||reg||10
Z||000007||webbee||07-18-2000||09:58 PM||||WOW x 2....  <P>How hard was the seat rebuild? How good is the leather quality on the seats? I want to go to leather on mine. Did you have to do the steering wheel? If so by who?<P>Just a great looking job!!!!!!||||reg||14
Z||000008||Old Lar||07-18-2000||10:02 PM||||I love it when someone saves a Fiero.  It does look nice!<P>I can not imagine how Pontiac can improve the basic style of the fast back.  The syle looks as good today as it did in 1986 when that design first came out.||||reg||14
Z||000009||mrfixit58||07-18-2000||10:02 PM||||I didn't get to watch the seat covers go on. But my Bro-n-law said it was simple. Now, to put that in prospective, he's a great fisherman and cook but, he is slightly "mechanically challenged". If he can do it, anyone can! <P>As far as the quality, Mr. Mike's is GREAT!<P>Sleepy now... off to bed...<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||6
